{
  "_id": "2aB45fUcIgu0Wx0NMULlU8VH7KK",
  "_type": "Doc",
  "_index": "Zx",
  "title": "Media",
  "navigationTitle": "",
  "body": [
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "A media root holds the images and files editors upload. Add one to a "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "workspace",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "2aAy4B81RXHCA8y06tSaep6CBen",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "259EzPfnSUaKOrNL1S2bpIpMdKl"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": " with `Config.media()` and set the workspace's `mediaDir` to the folder the files are written to. Link to uploads with the "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Image",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "3JkF0BPKV5b3VAoiTnAnsxh58Xi",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "Xu4-sW6S0ynehY5zKR1VZ"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "File",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "3JkF08RmGMh0aUQ7lI8Gm20TX78",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "tlhZ01MHUjv3Od172Ew6w"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Link",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "3JkF08zJLB1ot2n8cdr9uqVtLzp",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "24yE79dE2ssYPDQQHFFgT0eg2tH"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": " fields."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "CodeBlock",
      "_id": "2aB4BmlaljcbjYyF3KAxVvZgLhW",
      "code": "import {Config} from 'alinea'\n\nexport const main = Config.workspace('My site', {\n  source: 'content',\n  mediaDir: 'public/media',\n  roots: {\n    pages: Config.root('Pages'),\n    media: Config.media()\n  }\n})",
      "fileName": "",
      "language": "tsx"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Editors upload files in the media root of the dashboard and organize them in folders."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "What's stored"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "whats-stored"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Every upload is saved in two places:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "bulletList",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "The file itself goes to `mediaDir`, named after the original file plus the id of its entry: `public/media/landscape.2V4c3kRS.jpg`."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "A media entry is stored with your content, in the media root: `content/media/landscape.json`. It holds the title, the file location, the extension and size, a content hash and, for images, the width and height, the average color, a thumbhash placeholder, the focal point and the alt text."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Folders are entries too. Links store the id of the media entry, so moving or renaming a file in the dashboard doesn't break them."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Urls"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "urls"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Your site serves uploads at `/admin/file/<folders>/<name>.<extension>`, below the `adminPath` of your config. `withAlinea` forwards those requests to your Alinea handler, which serves the public copy of the file. When a file is moved or renamed, its old url keeps working. Set `mediaUrl` on the workspace to add a prefix, for example when two workspaces could have files with the same name."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "So keep `mediaDir` inside your public folder, and don't change it once there are uploads: entries store file locations relative to it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Options"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "options"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`Config.media(options)` takes the same options as "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`Config.root`",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "3JkF0CHOgF4k0wzcKLO1ub2XWH8",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "28hcdyq0sGJdgY6kM24NZd1XP5S"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": ", with media-specific behaviour:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "bulletList",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "`i18n`: translate the alt text of files. Files themselves aren't localised: every locale uses the same file, and editors enter an alt text per locale. Image links return the alt text in the locale of the entry you queried. Add a `fallback` function to choose which locales to try when a translation is missing: `fallback: locale => ['en']`."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "`children`: folders that always exist."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "`icon`, `orderChildrenBy` and `view`, as for other roots."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "The label of a media root is always \"Media\". A workspace can have several media roots; uploads that don't target a specific folder go to the first one."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Limits and production"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "limits-and-production"
    },
    {
      "_type": "bulletList",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "Set `maxUploadSize` in your "
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "config",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "_type": "link",
                      "_id": "3JkF0Cz04DRhmdKFUl8inbs4ovZ",
                      "_link": "entry",
                      "_entry": "259Ey7LXgqL7ZDGJ8XK1vBJmZrh"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": " (in bytes) to refuse larger uploads."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "Committing uploads to Git works well for images and documents, less so for large videos. When you deploy with your own backend, uploads can go to S3-compatible storage instead, see "
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "Self-hosted",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "_type": "link",
                      "_id": "3JkF07GARQwQU3N88zK66n8WCY5",
                      "_link": "entry",
                      "_entry": "2YlEGKqhO4mqRqEwQexeqRI8Jfu"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
